failure_location.quote:
Fix  a bounded domain $\Omega\subset \rrd$ and define the dictionary 
    $\bb{D}_\Omega $ 
    as follows:
    \begin{equation}\label{eq:D-Omega}
         \bb{D}_\Omega = \{ x \mapsto \sigma\left(\tfrac{\eta\cdot x}{\tau}+b\right)
        \varphi(\tfrac{\eta\cdot x}{\tau}+b-t)\phi(x-y) \text{ such that }(y,\eta, b) \in\Omega\times\rr{d}\times \rr{}\}

Then the short-time Fourier transform $V_\varphi\sigma$ never vanishes:
\[
V_\varphi \sigma(x,\omega) \;\neq\; 0 \qquad \text{for all }\;(x,\omega)\in\rr{2}.
\]
Moreover, we have the strict lower bound
\begin{equation}\label{eq:lowerbound}
\bigl|V_\varphi \sigma(x,\omega)\bigr|
\;>\; \frac{1}{2\pi}\,e^{-\pi x^2}
\qquad \text{for all }\;(x,\omega)\in\rr{2}.
\end{equation}
